Id: boot005w
Severity: WARN
Category: boot
Check: check_lilo
Fix: Run Tigris as root so the boot loader's configuration can be read.
References: grub-mkconfig(8); lilo.conf(5)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST AC-3, CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

Neither LILO's nor GRUB's configuration file could be read, so the boot
loader checks were not done.

The files looked for are /etc/lilo.conf, /boot/grub/grub.cfg and
/boot/grub2/grub.cfg (GRUB 2), and GRUB Legacy's /etc/grub.conf,
/boot/grub/menu.lst and /boot/grub/grub.conf. On a running system it
is reported only on x86, where one of them is to be expected; a
machine that boots with systemd-boot or straight from the firmware
has none, and this can be accepted.
